From Cursor:

I found the “global search” page and the search input. It currently does not auto-focus the search box on load.

Code reference (current input field):

show.html.haml









= text_field_tag :q, params[:q], placeholder: I18n.t(''global_searches.show.search_placeholder'', default: ''Search...'', skip_lit: true)
= draw_icon(''magnifying-glass'', class: ''input-icon'')
= submit_tag t(''.search'', default: ''Search''), name: :search, hidden: true



Answer

- No: As implemented, the cursor is not moved into the search box automatically.

- Quick fix: Add autofocus: true to the text_field_tag.

Proposed edit:





= text_field_tag :q, params[:q], placeholder: I18n.t(''global_searches.show.search_placeholder'', default: ''Search...'', skip_lit: true), autofocus: true



Alternative (if you prefer JS control): focus in the Stimulus controller on connect.









// app/javascript/controllers/global_search_controller.js
static targets = [''searchForm'', ''query''];
connect() { this.queryTarget?.focus(); }



And mark the input as a target in HAML:





= text_field_tag :q, params[:q], placeholder: I18n.t(''global_searches.show.search_placeholder'', default: ''Search...'', skip_lit: true), data: { global_search_target: ''query'' }



