Hi Kacper,



Please find attached the API description of the API and a postman collection for easily testing the endpoints. 



Note that this is our test-environment so while it should generally be stable and working, there might be outages because we are working on other projects at the same time. 



A few notes: 

- In the collection, a client ID and client secret for generating tokens is included. These have been setup by me in the test-environment. In the production environment, you will have access to the backoffice where you can create and revoke these secrets. 
- You can choose between “en” and “da” as language. However, in the account I’m using, there are multiple projects with English as language, so you must specify a project_id field as well, as shown below:This shouldn’t be an issue in production, since normally, you would only have one test (i.e., project) per language. In any case, it can be handled by adding the project_id field. If you omit the field, you will get helpful error message. 
- Since it is the test-environment, there is a possibility to generate the answers, so you don’t have to go through all the statements before testing that the callback works. Simply press “Mock answers” to do so:
- If you send report to both candidate and company, you will notice that both parties receive the same email, i.e., they can see each other’s email addresses. This is a known bug that we will fix – they should be sent separately.
- If you choose to send report to candidate or company (or both), you will also notice that there will be a delay between receiving the mail with a link to the report and receiving the information through the callback. The reason for this is that we need to generate the PDF, and this happens in a job that runs every 10 minutes or so. Hopefully, this isn’t an issue.



Enjoy testing and let me know of any issues you run into.



