A new tab called “Equipment & Assets” is added to each employee profile. It allows HR or managers to easily register, track, and manage all company-issued items — such as cars, laptops, phones, workwear, and access keys.



📋 Structure and Fields

Each issued item appears as a row in a clear, table-based layout with the following columns:

FieldDescriptionExampleCategoryType of asset (car, computer, phone, clothing, access, etc.)LaptopDescriptionShort item descriptionMacBook Pro 14" M2Serial number / IDSerial, IMEI, license plate, etc.SN: MBP2023-8453Issued dateWhen the item was handed out12-02-2024Returned dateWhen the item was returned (optional)01-10-2025StatusAutomatically updated (Active / Returned)ActiveCommentsNotes about condition or changesScreen replaced Apr 2025AttachmentUpload field for receipts, lease docs, etc.[Upload]



⚙️ Functionality

- Add new item: Quick entry form (category, details, dates).
- Auto status updates: When a return date is added, the item switches to “Returned.”
- Filter and sorting: Filter by category or status.
- Reports: Export asset lists for departments or individual employees.



🎨 Design

- Matches Elvium’s clean blue-white-orange UI.
- “+ Add item” button styled consistently with existing actions.
- Status badges (green for Active, gray for Returned).
- Small icons for edit ✏️, mark returned 📦, delete 🗑️.



  Reporting

- In the Elvium reporting module a new report should be added “Assets”
- Report will show all assets
- If an employee has been terminated and assets have not been returned whey will shown in red
- Collumns: Categori, description, employee name, status
- When clicked user is transferred to employee asset section



✅ Benefits

- Full visibility into all assigned equipment.
- Simplifies onboarding and offboarding.
- Prevents losses and keeps audit trails clear.
- Integrated into existing employee records — no separate tracking system needed.



